<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Windy Peak Traverse (Camp Windy Connector), from Pocket Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:206-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.329021" lon="-121.586759"><ele>1162.9</ele><name>Pocket Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:pocket-creek-sno-park (OSM node 6287637025); confidence: high; pdf_page: 206; book_elev_ft: 3800; quote: From Pocket Creek Sno-Park, 13 miles around Hood from Government Camp, ski east on the almost level road 0.6 mile to a bridge crossing of the East Fork</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.302220" lon="-121.603446"><ele>1288.4</ele><name>Upper Junction</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_204-1: OSM junction of Forest Road 3540 and Forest Road 3540-640; DEM 4,227 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 206; book_elev_ft: 4200; quote: to a road junction, hereafter referred to as the "Upper Junction," 2.7 miles from the trailhead</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.295170" lon="-121.593280"><ele>1428.4</ele><name>Mount Adams view clearcut</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_205-3: OSM node 3713226242, Forest Road 3540-640 at the foot of 3540-641, 1.36 mi from the Upper Junction; DEM 4,686 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 208; book_elev_ft: 4640; quote: ski up the upper Pocket Creek road, around the big bend into a large, rectangular clearcut (pdf 193: 'directly down 1,100 feet to the "Mount Adams view clearcut" on the upper Pocket Creek road')</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.296500" lon="-121.590500"><ele>1491.4</ele><name>Top, northeast corner of the clearcut</name><desc>source: placed upslope (east) of road 640 just past the 641 turnoff; the clearcut's edge is not mapped; DEM about 4,890 ft; confidence: low; pdf_page: 208; quote: Climb to the top, northeast corner of the clearcut, enter forest, and zigzag upward</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.295000" lon="-121.583000"><ele>1744.6</ele><name>Saddle north of Windy Peak</name><desc>source: DEM col on Gunsight Ridge between Windy Peak (DEM high 5,795 ft at 45.2921,-121.5847, the book's Point 5801) and the crest rising north to 5,830; DEM 5,722 ft, flat for about 150 m; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 208; quote: zigzag upward to the flat, forested saddle north of Windy Peak</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.293000" lon="-121.582300"><ele>1736.7</ele><name>East slope below the saddle</name><desc>source: placed on the open east flank, round the east side of Windy Peak; DEM 5,696 ft; confidence: low; pdf_page: 193; quote: From Camp Windy climb generally open slopes to the broad saddle just north of Windy Peak (Point 5801)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.291300" lon="-121.583000"><ele>1705.8</ele><name>Foot of the east slope</name><desc>source: placed in the basin north-east of the junction; DEM 5,595 ft; confidence: low; pdf_page: 208; quote: Another reward is the descent on open slopes to Camp Windy</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.289979" lon="-121.586767"><ele>1704.5</ele><name>Camp Windy</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_190-1: OSM node 3667973324, where Camp Windy Trail #685B leaves Gunsight Trail #685; DEM 5,592 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 192; quote: Camp Windy is located 1 mile northeast of Bonney Junction at the head of Boulder Creek. It is little more than several open slopes with scattered trees in a wide, gentle basin sloping eastward.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Windy Peak Traverse (Camp Windy Connector), from Pocket Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>1. Pocket Creek Sno-Park -&gt; Upper Junction: osm (high), 2.66 mi | 2. Upper Junction -&gt; Mount Adams view clearcut: osm (high), 1.32 mi | 3. Mount Adams view clearcut -&gt; Top, northeast corner of the clearcut: straight (low), 0.16 mi | 4. Top, northeast corner of the clearcut -&gt; Saddle north of Windy Peak: straight (low), 0.38 mi | 5. Saddle north of Windy Peak -&gt; East slope below the saddle: straight (low), 0.14 mi | 6. East slope below the saddle -&gt; Foot of the east slope: straight (low), 0.12 mi | 7. Foot of the east slope -&gt; Camp Windy: straight (medium), 0.20 mi</desc>
